  "term": "Golgi apparatus",
  "definition": "The Golgi apparatus is a cell structure involved in moving secretory cargo and in glycosylation, a major process that modifies proteins after they are made. In the source, disruption of Golgi-related O-glycosylation led to Golgi stress, and the Golgi apparatus later became disassembled as cell-death pathways were activated.",
